THOUGHT: The field is annotated @Nullable while the getter returns a non-null type, causing the NullAway error. Since initialize() is intended to set this before use, the safest fix is to enforce non-null at the getter by throwing if it hasn’t been initialized, which satisfies NullAway without changing the public signature. I’ll update the getter accordingly and then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/conductor && sed -i '32,34c\    public static MetadataDAO getMetadataDAO() {
        if (metadataDAO == null) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("ValidationContext.metadataDAO has not been initialized");
        }
        return metadataDAO;
    }' core/src/main/java/com/netflix/conductor/validations/ValidationContext.java && ./gradlew conductor-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -i "NullAway" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

